# annotation-of exposes both doc: and return: from @[...] function annotations (B-406).
# doc: is evaluated (including triple-quoted strings via [unindent "..."]).
# return: is exposed as a string representation of the return type annotation.
[f: [fn@[return: Number  doc: "Adds one to the input"] [let x@Int] [+ x 1]]]
[ann: [annotation-of f]]
[result-doc: [= ann.doc "Adds one to the input"]
 result-ret: [= ann.return "Number"]]
=== out
Dict({"result-doc": Bool(true), "result-ret": Bool(true)})
